# Issue #228 — internal audit/certification/reference material is repository-only.
# AUDIT_REPORT.md and FIELD_TEST_CHECKLIST.md were externally observed returning
# HTTP 200 on the app origin. wrangler.jsonc publishes `assets.directory: "."`,
# so anything NOT listed here is served, and these are documents about how the
# app is built, audited and certified — never something a driver's browser
# fetches. None of them is in the declared runtime inventory
# (scripts/lib/deploy-assets.mjs), which is what tests/unit/deploy-asset-coverage
# DAC-02 checks in the other direction.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: `field-certification.html` / `field-certification.js`
# are the operator-approved SAME-ORIGIN device companion and must stay fetchable
# on the real iPhone; `vendor/` carries the bundled SheetJS the service worker
# precaches.
AGENTS.md
AUDIT_REPORT.md
FIELD_TEST_CHECKLIST.md
RECON_24_0_2.md
UI_BRIEF_V24.5.md
FreightLogic_UI_Reference.html

# Repository-only directories: source of the gates, not inputs to the app.
.agents/
.claude/
.github/
.githooks/
docs/
schemas/
scripts/
tests/

# Observed 2026-09-23: the driver origin served `/admin-console/` (the Admin
# Console UI and its worker.js) and `native-ios/*`. The Admin Console is
# deployed to its OWN origin from `admin-console/` with its own .assetsignore;
# this root file only governs the driver origin, which must never carry an admin
# surface (#231). `native-ios/` is frozen repository-only Swift source.
admin-console/
native-ios/
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
